flowchart LR
    A[File I/O Performance] --> B[Synchronization]
    
    B --> C[fsync fd]
    B --> D[fdatasync fd]
    B --> E[sync]
    
    C --> C1[Flush file data + metadata]
    C --> C2[Waits for disk write]
    C --> C3[Expensive - use sparingly]
    
    D --> D1[Flush file data only]
    D --> D2[Skip timestamp updates]
    D --> D3[Faster than fsync]
    
    E --> E1[Flush all dirty buffers]
    E --> E2[System-wide]
    
    F[O_SYNC flag] --> F1[Every write() waits for disk]
    F --> F2[Slow but durable]
    
    G[O_DIRECT flag] --> G1[Bypass page cache]
    G --> G2[Databases use this]
    G --> G3[Must align to block size]
    
    H[Performance Tips] --> H1[Batch writes before fsync]
    H --> H2[Use fdatasync when possible]
    H --> H3[Consider data loss risk]
    H --> H4[Profile before optimizing]
    
